<ol><li>Subtraction trick vs Integer.compare — know both, prefer Integer.compare</li></ol>
<ol><li>return +1/0/-1 always — dangerous tricks; JVM never validates your logic</li></ol>
<h2>Quick reference card</h2>
<h3>TreeSet constructor decision tree</h3>
<p>Need TreeSet?
│
├─ Have existing Collection to convert?
│   └─ new TreeSet(collection) → natural sort applied
│
├─ Need default natural order (Comparable objects)?
│   └─ new TreeSet() → JVM calls compareTo()
│
└─ Need custom order?
    └─ new TreeSet(new MyComparator()) → JVM calls compare()</p>
<h3>compare() return contract (same as compareTo)</h3>
<h3>String Comparator recipes</h3>
